9          | PURPOSE:                                                                              |
10         |     The purpose of this program is to check data characteristics and quality of the   |
11         |	  SCDM-formatted Mother-Infant Linkage table.					|
12         |	  Prior to conducting a statistical 		                                        |
13         |	  query, sufficient data screening methods should be used for all variables to 		|
14         |	  identify miscoded, missing, or otherwise disorganized data. Some of the items 	|
15         |	  to check for include: missing required fields, validating values, validating 		|
16         |	  dates or dateranges, validating data types, etc.                                  |
17         |                                                                                       |
18         |     Data are generated from health plan administrative claims data held by Data       |
19         |     Partners into the SCDM.  Analytic models and monitoring are dependent on data,    |
20         |     which are both high in quality and contain a broad representation of the          |
21         |     population. To ensure the data will meet these goals, the Sentinel Operations     |
22         |     Center (SOC) has written this program to perform both data quality checks and to  |
23         |     profile the data to expose the breadth and depth of that data. This program       |
24         |     defines the data check process, the specific checks that will be performed and    |
25         |     how flagged data will be identified.                                              |
26         |---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
27         | PROGRAM INPUT:                                                                        |
