94        +
95        +The “Common Components” method makes site-specific metadata (e.g., data table names,
96        +folder locations, ETL facts) available to programs distributed to the
97        +Sentinel Distributed Network .  Each Sentinel data partner has a SAS file called
98        +“ms_common_components.sas” that assigns site-specific values to standard macro variables.
99        +
100       +The common components file contains macro variables that define attributes such as:
101       +* Data partner description variables
102       +* Most recent approved ETL version number
103       +* Min and Max dates corresponding to the time window with complete data for most recent
103      !+ETL
104       +* Key Sentinel directory paths
105       +* MSCDM table names
106       +* SAS Module Yes/No Flags
107       +
108       +Some ETL related metadata (e.g. ETL version and Min/Max dates) are automatically derived
108      !+from
109       +the ETL metadata produced from the QA package, while other ETL related metadata (e.g.
109      !+directory
110       +paths) need to be defined explicitly by the data partner
111       +
112       +Please consult as needed with your local contacts for MSCDM maintenance/QA review for
112      !+assistance with
113       +obtaining the directory paths needed for the macro variables _mscdm, _qaresults, and
113      !+_staging
